# 🔒 Data & Privacy Governance Policy (PCPD / GDPR / ISO 42001)

**Scope:** Ingestion, Processing, Storage, and Vectorization of Data  
**Compliance Standards:** HK PDPO (Cap. 486), EU GDPR, ISO/IEC 42001 Clause 7.5  

---

## 1. Data Processing Architecture
The system enforces a **Zero Data Retention (ZDR)** and **Local-First Architecture**.

\\\
[User Input] ➔ [PII Auto-Masking Engine] ➔ [Local Embedding / RAG Retrieval] ➔ [In-Memory Session Processing] ➔ [Instant Session Destruction]
\\\

## 2. Data Governance Rules

### A. Data Minimization & PII Isolation
* **No Raw PII Storage**: System never stores names, Hong Kong Identity Card (HKID) numbers, credit card details, or phone numbers in persistent storage.
* **Regex Pre-Processing**: Inputs containing PII are automatically redacted (`[REDACTED_PII]`) before hitting the vector database or model endpoints.

### B. Intellectual Property & Copyright Compliance
* **Copyrighted Material**: Only licensed, open-source, or corporate-owned documents may be vectorized into the RAG repository.
* **Excluded Data Types**: Unlicensed proprietary books, restricted third-party legal databases, and unverified web scrapes are strictly banned from `.gitignore` tracked files.

### C. Local Vector Database Security
* **Access Control**: Vector indexes are encrypted at rest using AES-256.
* **Isolation**: Dev, Staging, and Production environments maintain completely separate API keys and database namespaces.

---

## 3. Data Subject Rights (DSR) Handling
Since the system operates under a **Session-Only Memory Protocol**, user session data is destroyed immediately upon tab/application termination. No persistent user query history is stored, natively satisfying the **Right to be Forgotten (Article 17 GDPR)**.

